    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 98,
        "text": "Hi, Dr. Chen. Thanks for meeting me to go over my academic tasks before the transition check.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "89a064e2aaac25f78796a18afc91055c89fec3c2da0c0e804824d4b8a8c021fa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 109,
        "sourceEnd": 202,
        "text": "Of course, Mia. Let's review your progress. You submitted three assignments this term, right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9ab95dd305c8699a0d7e8ba834242efe66e781133610a0e8e56eb7861379bece",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 208,
        "sourceEnd": 285,
        "text": "Actually, four. The last one was the lab report, which I handed in on Friday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "585636e5758eb9a544d1f71c1cf8983df1ee21c09a61850207c56b2c2e10be4a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 296,
        "sourceEnd": 392,
        "text": "Right, the lab report. I remember now. So, four assignments. And your presentation is next week?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d01b4cf25d7b9d71ed8da470d19e9e820e9be8464f070ae0b2250fa9e5806889",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 398,
        "sourceEnd": 457,
        "text": "Yes, it's on Wednesday. I'm a bit nervous about the timing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b277566387eb95c578b8beb988f8fdc02502b70b89c74dd8bc090771ac7a8b46",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 468,
        "sourceEnd": 632,
        "text": "That's normal. Let's look at your written work first. Your essay on renewable energy was strong, but I noticed some issues with articles and subject-verb agreement.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9c3c9ab671a372d664ed595e2e74124e38040dc3b58ca4f1b140769c567b913b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 638,
        "sourceEnd": 764,
        "text": "Yes, I saw your comments. I often forget to use 'the' before specific nouns, and sometimes the verb doesn't match the subject.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ca87d261645d82be9f0e711cc2e74c52049dba08e6f15b7acad62132db151c65",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 775,
        "sourceEnd": 952,
        "text": "Exactly. For example, you wrote 'The data shows' but it should be 'The data show' in academic writing, though both are accepted. More importantly, you need to check consistency.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "16943c657385c205cac8305025298c180392b3f59ec81fd4603cfa30dfbee47c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 958,
        "sourceEnd": 1005,
        "text": "I'll review those. What about my use of tenses?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3b4fd80e27434d7595764d4cbaefbaec4922a1de27b7d9880200eac0fc2ee118",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1016,
        "sourceEnd": 1164,
        "text": "You mixed past and present tense in your literature review. When you describe a study from 2010, use past tense, but for general facts, use present.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "184a2f2dc7667abd92646608a8d4d9dc5b65e263c3b4e095d3743bb175e32d07",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1170,
        "sourceEnd": 1199,
        "text": "Got it. And relative clauses?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "6d981ea9d697b08e61736a3a8ac43ebfccb91260db34996909dcf1058aa83817",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1210,
        "sourceEnd": 1395,
        "text": "You used some correctly, but there was one sentence where the relative pronoun was missing. Like 'The researcher conducted the experiment was from China' – it should be 'who conducted'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "af9601e96bcc6474e58dd6343b77d5940827f6ae7fed5a20ca6816e18795a13e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1401,
        "sourceEnd": 1431,
        "text": "Oh, I see. I'll practice more.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b97c0540aff53bc9026bb16fd054555cbe57442ee982dc668b9a1c74fe86e7ff",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1442,
        "sourceEnd": 1549,
        "text": "Also, your use of quantifiers. You wrote 'many research' instead of 'much research' or 'a lot of research'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "83fbbe13951e5c15a6969c895e284a13e45e8dc5b80b3d07937e8dbc62cb8b58",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1555,
        "sourceEnd": 1586,
        "text": "Right, research is uncountable.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "146adfc74261a4fb47ae8d20f61255481ba9ef4f46c965cb31d5f37e837aaafd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1597,
        "sourceEnd": 1730,
        "text": "Yes. Now, about the transition check. It's a short interview where you discuss your academic progress. It will take about 15 minutes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "ac5fa66ec192497d32a1d21a13f4d5cd5949f16a1d323b34e0ea8df421586a8c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1736,
        "sourceEnd": 1767,
        "text": "Will it include a writing task?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "d373d38743f5e3b173346aae1fc5099cccb421228c015f8e9a776b284f51caf9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1778,
        "sourceEnd": 1844,
        "text": "No, just speaking. But you need to bring a portfolio of your work.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3c44eef413db4482f06f1c9c44129ab275734bee803ddda17798389f7ac4b123",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1850,
        "sourceEnd": 1931,
        "text": "I have three essays and the lab report. Should I include the presentation slides?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "650822f58e31f5f6ad47032569fc73c945bf17c624e4cf1f697f3f94e5a9d62d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1942,
        "sourceEnd": 2014,
        "text": "Yes, include everything. The check is on the 25th, at 2 pm, in room 204.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "97a3d31f3e6868548f02cb0bc5e976d2a8b261b212c45f919258a2492120b334",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2020,
        "sourceEnd": 2044,
        "text": "Thank you. I'll prepare.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4c9497ae9eb3eff7c704fc8d7a8aea90d5527d13b9651ee0b7a5d0108cb66a42",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2055,
        "sourceEnd": 2154,
        "text": "One more thing: during the interview, they might ask about your weaknesses. Be honest but positive.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "83f501e4ccd78a7f1de8986c08070a8f04b3faab59e6b411416f8a2584f7771b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2160,
        "sourceEnd": 2189,
        "text": "I will. Thanks for your help.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "022a578c385c233ad86950880b99e5fd60caee2829f2624d8e3a118eff0320a4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
